{"task_id": "Mbpp/3", "solution": "def is_not_prime(number) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a given number is not prime.\n    Returns True for composite numbers, 1, 0, negative numbers, and non-integers; False for prime numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    import math\n\n    # Prime numbers are integers greater than 1. Non-integer numbers are not prime.\n    if number != int(number):\n        return True\n\n    # Convert to integer for prime checking logic.\n    n = int(number)\n\n    # Numbers less than 2 are not prime.\n    if n < 2:\n        return True\n\n    # Number 2 is prime.\n    if n == 2:\n        return False\n\n    # Even numbers greater than 2 are not prime.\n    if n % 2 == 0:\n        return True\n\n    # Check for odd factors from 3 up to the square root of n.\n    limit = int(math.sqrt(n))\n    for i in range(3, limit + 1, 2):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return True\n\n    # If no factors were found, the number is prime.\n    return False"}
