{"task_id": "Mbpp/259", "solution": "def maximize_elements(tuple1, tuple2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Maximizes elements of two input tuples containing nested numeric tuple pairs.\n    It compares corresponding elements position-wise and returns a new tuple with maximum values.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        pair1 = tuple1[i]\n        pair2 = tuple2[i]\n        max_pair = (max(pair1[0], pair2[0]), max(pair1[1], pair2[1]))\n        result.append(max_pair)\n    return tuple(result)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/261", "solution": "def division_elements(tuple1, tuple2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs element-wise division on two tuples and returns a new tuple with the results.\n    Assumes tuples are of equal length and contain numeric elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    results = []\n    for dividend, divisor in zip(tuple1, tuple2):\n        results.append(dividend // divisor)\n    return tuple(results)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/264", "solution": "def dog_age(age: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates a dog's age in dog years using a specific conversion formula.\n    The first two human years contribute 10.5 dog years each, and subsequent years contribute 4 dog years each.\n    \"\"\"\n    if age <= 2:\n        return int(age * 10.5)\n    else:\n        return 21 + (age - 2) * 4"}
